  "description": "The carriers a catalogue's shipping service may name (docs/protocol/network.md §4.18, catalogue version 2; the policies document's services[].carrier), and that an order's shipments name later: each carrier's id, name, the countries it carries parcels within (empty: worldwide), its kind (post: a country's postal operator; parcel: a parcel network; express: an express courier), whether its numbers follow the UPU S10 form (s10: two letters, nine digits, two letters, ^[A-Z]{2}[0-9]{9}[A-Z]{2}$, for its international items), the form every one of its tracking numbers takes, as a regular expression (number_pattern; null where it is not known, and then a number is only checked to be 4 to 40 letters, digits and hyphens), the address of its own public tracking page with {number} for the tracking number (tracking_url_template; null where that page does not take the number in its address), and the registrable domains its tracking pages are on (domains). A tracking link a business gives is shown only when it is on one of its carrier's domains, or is the carrier's template filled in. No carrier here is called by any API: the business buys and prints its own labels. An id is never removed or renamed.",
